igure>
<p>Several text-to-image models have been developed using this approach, su=
ch as OpenAI=E2=80=99s DALL-E=E2=80=AF[5] and Google=E2=80=99s Muse=E2=80=
=AF[6].</p>
<h4 id=3D"diffusion-models">Diffusion models</h4>
<p>First introduced in 2019=E2=80=AF[7], diffusion models gained mainstream=
 attention about three years later. They use a different approach for text-=
to-image generation by starting with random noise and gradually transformin=
g it into a clear image based on the text prompt. This process typically in=
volves a text encoder, such as OpenAI=E2=80=99s CLIP [8] or Google=E2=80=99=
s T5 [9], which converts the text prompt into an embedding. This embedding =
captures the meaning of the prompt and guides the diffusion model to genera=
te images that match it.<sup><a id=3D"user-content-fnref-1" data-footnote-r=
ef=3D"true" aria-describedby=3D"footnote-label" href=3D"https://bytebytego.=
com/courses/genai-system-design-interview/text-to-image-generation#user-con=
tent-fn-1">1</a></sup></p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
