<section data-footnotes=3D"true" class=3D"footnotes"><h2 class=3D"sr-only" =
id=3D"footnote-label">Footnotes</h2>
<ol>
<li id=3D"user-content-fn-1">
<p>In practice, we provide the diffusion model with additional conditioning=
 inputs, such as the timestep. This will be discussed further in the traini=
ng section. <a data-footnote-backref=3D"" aria-label=3D"Back to reference 1=
" class=3D"data-footnote-backref" href=3D"https://bytebytego.com/courses/ge=
nai-system-design-interview/text-to-image-generation#user-content-fnref-1">=
=E2=86=A9</a></p>
</li>
<li id=3D"user-content-fn-2">
<p>For simplicity, we omitted the timestep input to the diffusion model. Th=
is will be covered in more detail in the training section. <a data-footnote=
-backref=3D"" aria-label=3D"Back to reference 2" class=3D"data-footnote-bac=
kref" href=3D"https://bytebytego.com/courses/genai-system-design-interview/=
text-to-image-generation#user-content-fnref-2">=E2=86=A9</a></p>
</li>
<li id=3D"user-content-fn-3">
<p>For simplicity, we include only the noisy image, xt, and the timestep, t=
, as the input. As mentioned earlier, conditioning signals can also be incl=
uded as inputs. <a data-footnote-backref=3D"" aria-label=3D"Back to referen=
ce 3" class=3D"data-footnote-backref" href=3D"https://bytebytego.com/course=
s/genai-system-design-interview/text-to-image-generation#user-content-fnref=
-3">=E2=86=A9</a></p>
</li>
<li id=3D"user-content-fn-4">
<p>For simplicity, the embedding space is visualized in 2D. In reality, it =
is a d-dimensional space, where d represents the embedding size. <a data-fo=
otnote-backref=3D"" aria-label=3D"Back to reference 4" class=3D"data-footno=
te-backref" href=3D"https://bytebytego.com/courses/genai-system-design-inte=
rview/text-to-image-generation#user-content-fnref-4">=E2=86=A9</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
